You're tasked with identifying these high earners across all departments. Write a query to display the employee's 
name along with their department name and salary. In case of duplicates, sort the results of department 
name in ascending order, then by salary in descending order. If multiple employees have the same salary, then order them alphabetically.

/// SQL Solution

with rnk_total as (
select *,
dense_rank() over(partition by e.department_id order by e.salary desc) as rnk
FROM employee e 
join department d on d.department_id = e.department_id)

select department_name, name, salary 
from rnk_total 
where rnk <= 3
ORDER BY department_name ASC, salary DESC, name ASC;
